## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-calendar/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:updater, libs:cal). Same pattern as ea_cloud-superapp/libs/.
## Added 2026-08-09 — the FOURTH time this bit us, and the worst: libs/core and
## libs/updater happened to be tracked already, so nothing looked broken, while
## libs/cal (created later) was silently ignored from birth. The entire calendar
## engine — IcsParser, CalSync, CalendarStore, CalModels — plus the CalDAV/VTODO
## client had never been committed and existed only on one machine's disk.
## `git status` showed clean. If you add a new module under any libs/, check
## `git check-ignore` before trusting a clean status.
!ea_cloud-calendar/libs/
!ea_cloud-calendar/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-news/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:updater, libs:news). Added 2026-08-09 BEFORE the module
## existed, rather than after discovering it had never been committed — the
## four entries above were all written after the fact. If you scaffold a new
## app under a libs/ tree, add its exception here in the same commit as the
## scaffold and confirm with `git check-ignore`; a clean `git status` proves
## nothing when the rule is this broad.
!ea_cloud-news/libs/
!ea_cloud-news/libs/**
